{
  "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
  "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "After decades of urging by sentencing judges and the Sentencing Commission, Congress in 2018 enacted Section 403 of the First Step Act. The point of Section 403 was to override Deal against United States, which called for extraordinarily harsh mandatory-minimum sentences even for first-time offenders. In enacting this override, Congress had to balance two countervailing values: first, justice in sentencing, and, second, finality of judgments."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0000-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Amicus's interpretation produces an anomalous result which there is no evidence Congress intended, and it's one that is flatly contrary to its acknowledged purpose."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Would you make any distinction or do you think there's -- it's a better -- there is a better argument for pre-Act vacaturs as opposed to post-Act vacaturs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. HANSFORD",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 403 can reduce an offender's sentence by decades."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF MASHA G. HANSFORD ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT IN SUPPORT OF THE PETITIONERS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "amicus's historic fact interpretation excludes offenders based on a consideration that has, as Justice Jackson just indicated, little conceivable relevance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: As I understand\nyour -- your answer, it has nothing to do with\nfairness to these two defendants. It has to do\nwith the burden on the court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Hansford",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. HANSFORD: Yes. So the -- the\ncurrent universe of cases, there are 16\noffenders that we're aware of who have already\nbenefited from this interpretation. And then\nthere are eight additional ones that we're aware\nof who -- whose -- for --for whom this question\nis open."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Then, on Justice\nSotomayor's question, I just want to make sure."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Michael H. McGinley",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "MR. McGINLEY: Mr. Chief Justice, and\nmay it please the Court:\nPetitioners do not qualify for\nretroactive relief under Section 403(b) of the\nFirst Step Act. The plain text of that\nprovision says that Section 403(a)'s changes\napply to a pre-Act offense only if a sentence\nfor the offense has not been imposed as of the\ndate of enactment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McGinley",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "I think the relevant time according to the statutory language is as of the date of enactment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McGinley",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "If there's no other contextual clue, then I do think that that's the normal way it's interpreted. Here, there is a contextual clue that's quite explicit in the statutory text."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you concede that if that is what Congress was doing or wanted to do, that these Petitioners fall in the category of people who have yet to be sentenced for this offense?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Senators Durbin, Grassley, Booker, Lee",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0003-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 77,
        "start": 77
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "ask you about this brief we have from four members of Congress. So Senators Durbin, Grassley, Booker, Lee, these are not guys who link arms very often."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "McGINLEY",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0004-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "And so it's clear that Congress does at times want old sentencing regimes to apply."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c5f8ee9bdeb154575a7895973e3a15cf91cfeeadd5647ab17e5bdd6689ff527",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c5f8ee9bdeb-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Mr. McGinley, would you agree that the -- the present-perfect tense usually refers to something that has continuing effect?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1002",
